silm:instances_papers_11_base_commutative_diagram_chapters_03_cheese_face_and_siblings_sections_03_cheese_face_F11_extended_treatment_concrete_anchor_22_CheeseTrapFace#cheesetrapface silm:hasLongDescription "The CheeseTrapFace is the rejected sentence pattern where unrestricted prose enters in olog position. In the paper's apparatus it appears as the symbol 'CheeseTrapFace', a concrete instance grounded in the Mittens domain story; it serves as the anchor whose semantics every diagram, formula, and prose reference back to." .
